                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8a5f0991-042e-4b29-9889-eff48cb91216",
                        "source_entry_id": "50225916-d4a7-3af6-93b0-0ef9dde9bc31",
                        "source_sense_id": "0cff4531-43c6-3658-bf0b-442687c3d2df",
                        "source_sense_description": "Selbstgefälligkeit, spöttisch-überhebliche Art",
                        "target_lang_word": "presumption",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "presumption",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "618c953b-16e7-3963-a309-384594cd286e",
                                        "entry_id": "8f5fb803-9114-338f-901a-ced5f9ce7a21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of presuming, or something presumed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "feb48426-af2b-4ba2-9c94-a05196cf2806",
                                                "sense_id": "618c953b-16e7-3963-a309-384594cd286e",
                                                "text": "Yet, in contradiction to all these very plausible presumptions, even this remote period teems with its own peculiar and separate instruction."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "64539266-7ad0-30ef-8d0d-b0f9f1f7e398",
                                        "entry_id": "8f5fb803-9114-338f-901a-ced5f9ce7a21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The belief of something based upon reasonable evidence, or upon something known to be true."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "622a685b-6337-436d-ab14-9086bd842253",
                                                "sense_id": "64539266-7ad0-30ef-8d0d-b0f9f1f7e398",
                                                "text": "The presumption is that an event has taken place."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd07a88e-711c-4388-81b2-0dd944927139",
                                                "sense_id": "64539266-7ad0-30ef-8d0d-b0f9f1f7e398",
                                                "text": "I have here imputed the Continuance of the War to the mutual Indulgence between our General and Allies, wherein they both so well found their Accounts; to the Fears of the Mony-changers, left their Tables should be overthrown; to the Designs of the Whigs, who apprehended the Loss of their Credit and Employments in a Peace; and to those at home, who held their immoderate Engrossments of Power and Favour, by no other Tenure than their own Presumption upon the Necessity of Affairs."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "367604cb-34f5-3452-895a-818fa84d1035",
                                        "entry_id": "8f5fb803-9114-338f-901a-ced5f9ce7a21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The condition upon which something is presumed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cba33727-6066-331e-a307-a385b78eec75",
                                        "entry_id": "8f5fb803-9114-338f-901a-ced5f9ce7a21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Arrogant behaviour; the act of venturing beyond due bounds of reverence or respect."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "dated",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "526164d1-60cd-421d-990c-49ac501c2b78",
                                                "sense_id": "cba33727-6066-331e-a307-a385b78eec75",
                                                "text": "Note the preſumption of this Scythian ſlaue:\nI tel thee villaine, thoſe that lead my horſe\nHaue to their names tytles of dignitie,\nAnd dar’ſt thou bluntly cal me Baiazeth?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e6b7b03a-6b40-4508-8073-f70ce0b1af6a",
                                                "sense_id": "cba33727-6066-331e-a307-a385b78eec75",
                                                "text": "Thy son I killed for his presumption."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20d0c116-aaf9-489a-a12c-42507cc484a2",
                                                "sense_id": "cba33727-6066-331e-a307-a385b78eec75",
                                                "text": "[…]yet even then, I had the preſumption to Dedicate to your Lordſhip: A very unfiniſh'd Piece […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d5ee1e62-1450-40f2-8ad9-f8a6e6d77e71",
                                                "sense_id": "cba33727-6066-331e-a307-a385b78eec75",
                                                "text": "“Let me be rightly understood. This match, to which you have the presumption to aspire, can never take place. No, never. Mr. Darcy is engaged to my daughter. Now what have you to say?”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "872e3270-07fe-4c2c-97a4-8437eff7647c",
                                                "sense_id": "cba33727-6066-331e-a307-a385b78eec75",
                                                "text": "“If I had not persuaded Harriet into liking the man, I could have borne any thing. He might have doubled his presumption to me—but poor Harriet!”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6cad5f43-d97a-32af-8a3b-2f862d8a1312",
                                        "entry_id": "8f5fb803-9114-338f-901a-ced5f9ce7a21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An inference that a trier of fact is either permitted or required to draw under certain factual circumstances (as prescribed by statute or case law) unless the party against whom the inference is drawn is able to rebut it with admissible, competent evidence."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2969470d-786a-4a83-9701-ed4cb15eac4c",
                                                "sense_id": "6cad5f43-d97a-32af-8a3b-2f862d8a1312",
                                                "text": "The state, in the exercise of its general power to prescribe rules of evidence, may provide that proof of a particular fact, or of several facts taken collectively, shall be prima facie evidence of another fact when there is some rational connection between the fact proved and the ultimate fact presumed. The legislative presumption is invalid when it is entirely arbitrary, or creates an invidious discrimination, or operates to deprive a party of a reasonable opportunity to present the pertinent facts in his defense."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a91ab994-19e6-4bf6-beba-34f5dfcbcf0e",
                        "source_entry_id": "50225916-d4a7-3af6-93b0-0ef9dde9bc31",
                        "source_sense_id": "0cff4531-43c6-3658-bf0b-442687c3d2df",
                        "source_sense_description": "Selbstgefälligkeit, spöttisch-überhebliche Art",
                        "target_lang_word": "suffisance",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "suffisance",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "82e886bc-853d-3fe5-ac6e-e50d7f252ef1",
                                        "entry_id": "c5fd20c5-f1a9-3de9-97a1-6e3a64d1d303",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ce qui suffit, ce qui est assez."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d4d2ac6b-00ec-4533-bac1-67cd68325387",
                                                "sense_id": "82e886bc-853d-3fe5-ac6e-e50d7f252ef1",
                                                "text": "Il n’y a aucune exagération à alléguer que, pour la première fois dans l’histoire de l’humanité, les populations se trouvaient approvisionnées plus qu’à leur suffisance, […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bc10bc94-5c86-4d6b-8226-b74009b9df88",
                                                "sense_id": "82e886bc-853d-3fe5-ac6e-e50d7f252ef1",
                                                "text": "Cette cérémonie assurait des pluies en suffisance pour l'ensemble des villages limitrophes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7a6f773e-9d3b-470b-901c-d427fbabc1bb",
                                                "sense_id": "82e886bc-853d-3fe5-ac6e-e50d7f252ef1",
                                                "text": "Les pays en développement n'en produisant guère, en tous cas pas en suffisance, les produits pharmaceutiques doivent le plus souvent être importés."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e307eaa-fa3b-465e-aacf-bbeab4437bda",
                                                "sense_id": "82e886bc-853d-3fe5-ac6e-e50d7f252ef1",
                                                "text": "Il avait sa suffisance de la vue de sa maussade belle-sœur sous ses harnais de joyaux …."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c225a17c-b0ad-3aad-b96d-99302672e5b0",
                                        "entry_id": "c5fd20c5-f1a9-3de9-97a1-6e3a64d1d303",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Vanité, satisfaction de soi, présomption impertinente. Prétention à détenir la vérité sur un point de détail, ou à dicter la manière de faire."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6571659f-6d62-4773-85cb-ee5fdb0cfb38",
                                                "sense_id": "c225a17c-b0ad-3aad-b96d-99302672e5b0",
                                                "text": "Il observait la suffisance du chevalier de Beauvoisis, c’est ainsi qu’il s’était nommé en parlant de lui, choqué de ce que Julien l’appelait tout simplement monsieur."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a01a22a-9c43-4dd5-9ac2-3fae08dfa387",
                                                "sense_id": "c225a17c-b0ad-3aad-b96d-99302672e5b0",
                                                "text": "À son ton naturellement tranchant, il ajouta la suffisance d'un parvenu, et devint même ridicule, à force d’être impertinent."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da115b88-15ff-4975-8d75-4155f78ac241",
                                                "sense_id": "c225a17c-b0ad-3aad-b96d-99302672e5b0",
                                                "text": "Chef-d'œuvre de suffisance en même temps que d'insuffisance administrative, le plan 17, en un mot, recélait autant d’impéritie, dans la préparation, qu'en devait déceler le \"plan d’opérations\" dans sa conduite."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29a1d65f-839a-4817-92cd-4fa6b2287dd5",
                                                "sense_id": "c225a17c-b0ad-3aad-b96d-99302672e5b0",
                                                "text": "Mais nous ne verrons rien dans une pareille phrase qu'un mélange de mépris, d'insulte, de suffisance bourgeoise."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b55a150-45e8-4128-b2f7-6342980721e9",
                                                "sense_id": "c225a17c-b0ad-3aad-b96d-99302672e5b0",
                                                "text": "M'autorisez-vous, maintenant, s'informa-t-il, en affectant une rondeur pleine de suffisance, à évoquer l'atmosphère du crime ?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d0da4f0-9c06-4cd6-b389-a91bc4cfcd36",
                                                "sense_id": "c225a17c-b0ad-3aad-b96d-99302672e5b0",
                                                "text": "L'homme argue de son droit avec une suffisance presque impertinente, une humilité feinte qui voile une ironie bien claire : […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd79a1cd-2e35-4802-bc81-9b2da1710869",
                                                "sense_id": "c225a17c-b0ad-3aad-b96d-99302672e5b0",
                                                "text": "Je réclame, le droit à l'impertinence, à cause, monsieur le président, de votre arrogance, de votre suffisance, de votre mépris du peuple, des jojos, des moins que rien, des Gaulois réfractaires."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
